{"type": "complete", "response": "I don\u2019t have a way to read your computer\u2019s volume setting directly.\u202fIf you\u2019d like to check it yourself:\n\n**macOS**  \n1. Click the **sound** icon (\ud83d\udd0a) in the menu bar, or open **System Settings \u2192 Sound**.  \n2. The slider shows the current output volume (and you can adjust it there).\n\n**Windows**  \n1. Click the **speaker** icon in the task\u2011bar, or go to **Settings \u2192 System \u2192 Sound**.  \n2. The volume bar indicates the current level.\n\n**Linux (GNOME/KDE, etc.)**  \n1. Click the volume indicator in the panel, or open the **Sound** settings from your system menu.  \n2. The slider displays the current output level.\n\nLet me know if you need step\u2011by\u2011step help for a specific OS!", "session_id": "default", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model_key": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model_provider": "omniroute", "model_fallback_used": false, "model_fallback_reason": "", "model_latency_ms": 6611, "model_ttft_ms": 5524, "intent": "conversation", "goal_id": "", "state": "", "executive": {"intent": "conversation", "message": "I don\u2019t have a way to read your computer\u2019s volume setting directly.\u202fIf you\u2019d like to check it yourself:\n\n**macOS**  \n1. Click the **sound** icon (\ud83d\udd0a) in the menu bar, or open **System Settings \u2192 Sound**.  \n2. The slider shows the current output volume (and you can adjust it there).\n\n**Windows**  \n1. Click the **speaker** icon in the task\u2011bar, or go to **Settings \u2192 System \u2192 Sound**.  \n2. The volume bar indicates the current level.\n\n**Linux (GNOME/KDE, etc.)**  \n1. Click the volume indicator in the panel, or open the **Sound** settings from your system menu.  \n2. The slider displays the current output level.\n\nLet me know if you need step\u2011by\u2011step help for a specific OS!", "session_id": "default", "goal_id": "", "state": "", "result": {}, "context_sources": [], "model_provenance": {"provider": "